  partName: Right Outer Cover
  description: The Left Outer Cover is a large, elongated part situated at the middle-left-center
    of the engine, constructed from Outer cover material. Its primary role is to
    provide a protective and aerodynamic casing for the engine, shielding internal
    components while minimizing drag. Notably, its mirrored design with the Right
    Outer Cover enables a symmetrical and balanced engine configuration, optimizing
    performance and stability.
